# Hands-off installation on the live system: runs `dkrescue-install --auto` once at boot. Without `dkinstall.auto=1`
# on the kernel command line it prints "nothing to do" and exits 0 at once, so it is harmless on every boot; with the
# flag it looks for an answers file (install/answers.toml on the live medium, dkinstall.toml on a mounted or unmounted
# USB stick or disk, or the path in dkinstall.answers=) and, only if all the safety gates pass (the flag, a
# `confirm_erase` that names the disk to be wiped, never the live medium), installs without a screen and then reboots,
# powers off or leaves a shell (`when_done`). See docs/AUTOINSTALL.md in the dkinstaller source.
# Enabled by the live images (images/dkde.toml, images/rescue.toml); not by the package.
type    = scripted
command = /usr/sbin/dkrescue-install --auto
options: starts-on-console
depends-on: udev-settle
depends-on: loginready
